    "blurb": "Execute scripts within your processes",
    "overview": "The Script Connector lets you call any scripting language directly from a Camunda process. It ships with built-in support for JavaScript, Kotlin, Groovy, and Mustache, plus an extensible framework for registering custom scripting engines via SPI.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Execute any script from your Camunda processes",
    "splashDescription": "Teams migrating from Camunda 7 to Camunda 8 often depend on embedded scripts for lightweight business logic, but reproducing that flexibility in Camunda 8 can require significant rework. The Script connector lets you call any kind of script directly from a Camunda process, with built-in support for the scripting languages most commonly used in Camunda 7: JavaScript, Kotlin, Groovy, and Mustache. An extensible engine registration framework lets you plug in any additional JSR-223 compliant scripting language via SPI, so teams can preserve and extend existing logic without rewriting their process models.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/810748/overview/img1734796207572782182.png?e8483ec33a979b19caa827138e530e49",
